.TH UNIM-CLI 1 "November 2026" "UNIM 0.4.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-cli \- Korean/English keyboard converter and UNIM settings manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-cli
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B unim\-cli config
.RI [ SUBCOMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B unim\-cli dict
.IR user\-dict | blacklist | hanja
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unim\-cli
is a unified command-line tool that offers two modes of operation:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBText conversion\fR (default, when no subcommand is supplied):
an offline batch utility that converts between English keyboard
character streams and composed Hangul. It is independent of the running
.B unim\-daemon
\(em it processes its input as a pure layout transformation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSettings management\fR (via the \fBconfig\fR subcommand): reads and
writes the UNIM user configuration file
.RB ( ~/.config/unim/config.yaml ),
using the same configuration backend as the
.B unim\-gui\-gtk
settings dialog and the daemon itself. This is the recommended way to
script configuration changes from shell environments. Changes take
effect immediately for the running daemon via the
.B ConfigChanged
D-Bus signal; no restart is required.
.PP
With no input file in conversion mode, it reads from standard input. With
one or more
.I FILE
arguments, files are processed in order and concatenated to standard
output (or the file given via
.BR \-o ).
.SH CONVERSION OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compose
Compose an English keyboard stream into Hangul (default mode).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompose
Decompose Hangul into the equivalent English keyboard stream.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " "\-\-output \fIFILE\fR"
Write output to
.IR FILE
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " "\-\-korean\-keyboard \fILAYOUT\fR"
Korean keyboard layout. One of
.BR 2bul ", " 390 ", " 391 ", " noshift "."
Default:
.BR 2bul "."
.TP
.BR \-e ", " "\-\-english\-keyboard \fILAYOUT\fR"
English keyboard layout. One of
.BR qwerty ", " dvorak ", " colemak ", " colemak_dh ", " workman "."
Default:
.BR qwerty "."
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH CONFIG SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B config show
Print the current configuration summary to standard output.
.TP
.BR "config set" " \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR"
Set a single configuration key. Run
.B unim\-cli config set \-\-help
for the full list of supported keys (for example
.BR korean\-layout ", " english\-layout ", " default\-category ", "
.BR toggle\-keys ", " auto\-typefix ", "
and the
.B auto\-typefix\-*
family).
.TP
.B config path
Print the absolute path of the active configuration file.
.TP
.B config reset
Reset the configuration file to default values.
.TP
.B config interactive
Launch an interactive prompt-driven configuration session. Useful when a
graphical settings dialog is not available.
.SH DICT SUBCOMMANDS
The
.B dict
group manages the three word lists that UNIM reads from its configuration
directory. The files are read and written directly (not through the
daemon), and the running daemon picks up changes automatically.
.SS dict user\-dict
Reverse (Korean\->English) AutoTypeFix auto\-correction dictionary. Words
listed here are always corrected back to English.
.TP
.B dict user\-dict list
Print every registered word with its note.
.TP
.BR "dict user\-dict add" " \fIWORD\fR... [\fB\-\-note\fR \fINOTE\fR]"
Register one or more English words (letters only).
.TP
.BR "dict user\-dict remove" " [\fB\-y\fR] \fIWORD\fR..."
Remove words (case\-insensitive).
.TP
.B dict user\-dict clear
Delete all entries after confirmation.
.TP
.B dict user\-dict path
Print the file path
.RB ( typefix\-userdict.yaml ).
.SS dict blacklist
AutoTypeFix suppression dictionary (corrections the user undid).
.TP
.B dict blacklist list
Print the entries with their 1\-based index, status and key sequence.
.TP
.BR "dict blacklist remove" " [\fB\-y\fR] \fIINDEX\fR..."
Remove entries by the 1\-based indices shown by
.BR list .
.TP
.B dict blacklist clear
Delete all entries after confirmation.
.TP
.B dict blacklist path
Print the file path
.RB ( typefix\-blacklist.yaml ).
.SS dict hanja
Hanja user dictionary: names and terms that are missing from the built\-in
dictionary, as \fIhangul \-> hanja\fR (with an optional meaning). Candidates
are shown in the order bookmarks, user dictionary, built\-in dictionary.
Changes apply from the next Hanja key press; no restart is needed. The hanja
must have exactly as many characters as the hangul (1 to 18 syllables).
.TP
.BR "dict hanja list" " [\fIHANGUL\fR]"
Print all entries (or only those for
.IR HANGUL ).
Invalid entries are marked with a warning.
.TP
.BR "dict hanja add" " \fIHANGUL\fR \fIHANJA\fR [\fB\-\-meaning\fR \fIMEANING\fR]"
Add an entry after validation.
.TP
.BR "dict hanja edit" " \fIHANGUL\fR \fIHANJA\fR [\fB\-\-hangul\fR \fINEW\fR] [\fB\-\-hanja\fR \fINEW\fR] [\fB\-\-meaning\fR \fIMEANING\fR]"
Change the entry identified by the (HANGUL, HANJA) pair. An empty
.B \-\-meaning ""
clears the meaning. At least one option is required.
.TP
.BR "dict hanja remove" " \fIHANGUL\fR [\fIHANJA\fR] [\fB\-y\fR]"
Remove one entry. Without
.I HANJA
all entries for
.I HANGUL
are removed; with two or more a confirmation is asked
.RB ( \-y
skips it, and is required when not interactive).
.TP
.B dict hanja clear
Delete all entries after confirmation. If the file is unreadable it is first
renamed to
.B hanja\-userdict.yaml.broken\-\fIDATE\fR
instead of being overwritten.
.TP
.B dict hanja path
Print the file path
.RB ( hanja\-userdict.yaml ).
.PP
The exit status is 0 on success and 1 if any operation failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Convert a stream of QWERTY keystrokes to Hangul:
.PP
.RS
.nf
echo "dkssudgktpdy" | unim\-cli \-c
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decompose a Hangul file into Dvorak keystrokes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unim\-cli \-d \-e dvorak input.txt \-o keystrokes.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show current settings and change the Korean layout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unim\-cli config show
unim\-cli config set korean\-layout 3bul390
.fi
.RE
.PP
Register a name in the Hanja user dictionary:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unim\-cli dict hanja add 서기현 徐基鉉 \-\-meaning "my name"
unim\-cli dict hanja list
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
The configuration file managed by the \fBconfig\fR subcommand.
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/hanja\-userdict.yaml
The Hanja user dictionary managed by \fBdict hanja\fR.
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/typefix\-userdict.yaml
The auto\-correction dictionary managed by \fBdict user\-dict\fR.
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/typefix\-blacklist.yaml
The suppression dictionary managed by \fBdict blacklist\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-gui\-gtk (1)
